10
01:06:50,526 --> 01:06:56,526
Ghost is a 1990 American supernatural romance film directed by Jerry Zucker, written by Bruce Joel
Rubin, and starring Patrick Swayze, Demi Moore, Whoopi Goldberg, and Tony Goldwyn.

11
01:13:31,578 --> 01:13:37,578
It focuses on Sam Wheat (Swayze), a murdered banker, whose ghost sets out to save his girlfriend, Molly Jensen (Moore),
from the person who arranged his murder (Goldwyn) – through the help of the psychic Oda Mae Brown (Goldberg).

12
01:20:12,631 --> 01:20:18,631
Ghost was theatrically released on July 13, 1990 by Paramount Pictures, to commercial success, grossing $505 million against a budget of $22–23
million and emerging as the highest-grossing film of 1990 and at the time of its release, was the third-highest-grossing film of all time.

13
01:26:53,684 --> 01:26:59,684
The film was a sleeper hit, which unexpectedly outperformed several
blockbuster action films released during that summer.

14
01:33:34,736 --> 01:33:40,736
Its success extended to the home video market, and it was the
most rented film of 1991 in the United States.

15
01:40:15,789 --> 01:40:21,789
The film initially received mixed reviews from critics, with praise
going towards the score and performances of the cast.

16
01:46:56,842 --> 01:47:02,842
Ghost earned five nominations at the 63rd Academy Awards: Best Picture, Best Original Score, Best Film
Editing, and winning Best Supporting Actress for Goldberg and Best Original Screenplay for Rubin.

17
01:53:37,894 --> 01:53:43,894
The film explores themes of fortune teller, corruption,
soulmates, afterlife, money transfer.

18
02:00:18,947 --> 02:00:24,947
The tone is mind_bending and emotional and intense.
